Z||000008||WKDFIRO||09-01-2001||12:33 PM||||The "Bumble Bee" Fiero was actually a DOHC SD-4 that Pontiac was developing that would fit on a stock block, in theory.<P>It was actually fuel injected. <P>If you get a chance to read the article I would recommend it!||||reg||6
Z||000009||Oreif||09-01-2001||01:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by WKDFIRO:<BR><B>The "Bumble Bee" Fiero was actually a DOHC SD-4 that Pontiac was developing that would fit on a stock block, in theory.<P>It was actually fuel injected. <P>If you get a chance to read the article I would recommend it!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>The block is an SD4 also.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Pontiaddict||09-01-2001||10:06 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by IwannaIRM:<BR><B>Yes, onfire, that is the one that I am talking about.  Sweet ride.<P>The rear struts were modified Firebird Struts.  For running around town it was shod with 17x14.5(rear) and 17x12(front)wheels.<P>I think at the time of the article it ran a 13.7 in the quarter.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I remember reading the article, but I don't remember the 12" wide front wheels. I remember they used some lowering spindles made to put f-body hubs on them so they could use large bolt pattern rims on both ends (had a rear hub swap too).<p>[This message has been edited by Pontiaddict (edited 09-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||tomanyfieros||09-02-2001||11:24 AM||||hey, scan that article. would u like to sell that book? i have been looking for one, LMK<BR>Thanx Jason<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dreamer.gif">    <BR><B>We all have dreams, but not everyone gets them...</B>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Oreif||09-02-2001||11:52 AM||||I have a scanned version of the article. The only thing from Firebirds used was the rear struts. Which were modified to use smaller diameter springs for tire clearence. The wheels and tires were experimental versions from centerline and goodyear. The fronts were 17 X 4.5 and the rears were 17 X 12.<BR>(Yes they used skinny tires up front.)<BR>Tire sizes were:<BR>Front 155/70D17<BR>Rear 315/35VR17<BR>Neither were ever sold to the public. The car was built by Pontiac Motorsports Division as a technology demonstraitor.<BR>The engine was an SD4 block and SD 16-valve head with 8 injectors. Providing 273HP and 240 torque.<BR>As for times,<BR>0-60 was 5.36<BR>1/4 mile was 13.37<BR>top speed was 150+<BR>Exhaust was 4 straight pipes to a supertrapp muffler/tailpipe. <P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 09-02-2001).]||||reg||1
